    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "Find the equation of a circle with centre $(5,-2)$ passing through $(-1,1)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$(x-5)^2+(y+2)^2=45$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}r^2&=(-1-5)^2+(1+2)^2\\\\&=36+9\\\\&=45\\end{align*}$$\nThe distance between the centre and the point is $\\sqrt{45}$, so the radius is $\\sqrt{45}$.\n$$(x-5)^2+(y+2)^2=45$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
